page('services/new-construction.html','New Home Construction',twoimg('newhome-1.webp','newhome-2.webp','New Construction, Simplified','“From selecting the right builder to final walkthrough, I guide you through every step of buying a new home in Las Vegas confidently and stress free.”')+f'''<section class="bg-gray"><div class="wrap content"><h2>New Home Construction</h2><p>Buying a new construction home in Las Vegas doesn’t have to be overwhelming. I help you navigate builders, communities, floor plans, and design options so you can make confident decisions without the stress.</p><p>Whether you’re purchasing a quick move-in home or building from the ground up, I’ll guide you through the entire process and advocate for your best interests from start to finish.</p><h3>Why You Should Have Representation</h3><ul><li>The builder’s sales agent represents the builder—not you.</li><li>I negotiate pricing, upgrades, and available incentives.</li><li>I protect your interests from contract to closing.</li></ul><p>If you're considering new construction, Im happy to walk you through your options. {CM()} to get started.</p></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><div class="builders">{BLD}</div></div></section>''')
page('services/relocation.html','Relocation',hero('Your Las Vegas Move, Made Simple','“Whether you’re moving from another city or across the state, I make relocating to Las Vegas simple and stress free.”','assets/img/relocation-hero.webp')+f'''<section><div class="wrap content"><h2>Relocation Made Easy!</h2><p>Moving to Las Vegas? I’m here to make it smooth, stress free, and even exciting! Relocating to a new city can feel overwhelming, but with the right guidance, finding your new home can be a great experience.</p><h3>Buy Without Visiting</h3><p>I’ve helped many clients purchase homes sight unseen. I’ll guide you virtually through listings, inspections, and walk throughs. Handling the details so you can focus on your move.</p><h3>Find the Perfect Neighborhood</h3><p>Through a free Buyer’s Consultation, virtual or in person, we’ll explore your ideal community. You’ll get access to detailed guides, school info, crime maps, walk scores, and more to choose the right spot for your family.</p><h3>Connect with Local Services</h3><p>New to Las Vegas? I’ll help you get set up with utilities, trusted contractors, and other essential services. Making your transition seamless.</p><h3>Relocating Beyond Nevada</h3><p>If your move takes you outside of Nevada, I can also connect you with a trusted, reputable real estate agent anywhere in the country.</p><h3>Start Your Move Today</h3><p>{CM()} to schedule your free consultation and let’s find your perfect Las Vegas home!</p></div></section>''')
page('services/short-sale-foreclosure.html','Short Sale/ Foreclosure',twoimg('shortsale-1.webp','shortsale-2.webp','Short Sales &amp; Foreclosures in Las Vegas','Facing a short sale or foreclosure can feel overwhelming, but understanding your options is the first step. This guide helps Las Vegas homeowners navigate both short sales and foreclosures, outlining the process, timelines, and key considerations to make informed decisions with confidence.')+f'''<section class="bg-gray"><div class="wrap content"><h2>Understanding the Short Sale Process</h2><h3>What Is a Short Sale?</h3><p>A short sale happens when your Las Vegas home sells for market value, but that amount is less than what you currently owe on the mortgage. In these situations, the lender must approve the sale and agree to accept less than the full loan balance. Short sales are often an option for homeowners experiencing hardship and looking to avoid foreclosure.</p><h3>Short Sale vs. Foreclosure</h3><p>Foreclosure occurs when the lender takes control of the property and sells it at auction after missed payments. A short sale is different it allows you to stay in control of the sale process and can be far less damaging to your credit. Federal guidelines require lenders to wait before starting foreclosure, which can create a window of opportunity to pursue a short sale instead.</p><h3>Is It Too Late If I’ve Received a Notice?</h3><p>Not necessarily. Even if you’ve received a Notice of Default, you may still have time to list your home, secure an offer, and submit a complete short sale package to your lender. In many cases, once a short sale is under review, foreclosure proceedings may be postponed. Acting quickly is critical.</p><h3>How I Help With Short Sales</h3><p>Short sales involve strict timelines, detailed paperwork, and constant communication with lenders. I guide you through each step from evaluating your situation and preparing your home, to submitting accurate documentation and negotiating with the bank. Every short sale is different, but having the right strategy and representation can make a meaningful difference.</p><p>If you’re unsure whether a short sale is right for your situation, a quiet conversation can help bring clarity. I’m happy to review your options and answer questions {CM()} to go over your options.</p></div></section>''')
page('services/reverse-purchase.html','Reverse Purchase',f'''<section><div class="wrap split"><div><h1 style="color:#ED0677">Reverse Mortgage Home Sales in Las Vegas</h1><p>A reverse mortgage can be a helpful way to access your home’s equity, reduce monthly expenses, or supplement your income. This page explains how reverse mortgages work, how they are repaid, and what to consider when selling a home with a reverse mortgage giving you the clarity and guidance to make informed decisions with confidence.</p></div><img src="{{P}}assets/img/reverse-hero.webp" alt=""></div></section>
<section class="bg-gray"><div class="wrap content"><h2>Understanding Reverse Mortgages and Home Sales</h2><h3>What Is a Reverse Mortgage?</h3><p>If you’re 62 or older and live in the Las Vegas area, a reverse mortgage can help reduce monthly expenses while giving access to additional funds. It allows you to leverage your home’s equity to cover medical bills, home improvements, or supplement your income. Unlike traditional mortgages, the loan balance grows over time as the bank pays out funds.</p><h3>How Is It Repaid?</h3><p>Reverse mortgages are typically repaid when you sell your home, move out, or pass away. The lender recoups the balance from the home’s sale proceeds. If the home sells for more than the loan balance, any remaining equity goes to you or your heirs. Regular upkeep and property taxes must be maintained to keep the loan in good standing.</p><h3>Selling a Home with a Reverse Mortgage</h3><p>Because the loan balance can grow over time, selling a home with a reverse mortgage requires a Realtor experienced in the process. An expert agent can help highlight factors that preserve or enhance home value, ensuring a smooth sale even when the mortgage balance is high.</p><h3>What If the Home Has Lost Value?</h3><p>If your home’s market value is lower than the loan balance, a short sale may be required. Reverse mortgages are nonrecourse loans, so the lender cannot pursue you or your heirs for the difference between the loan and the sale price. The lender may request an appraisal before approving the sale, but the process is designed to protect you and your family.</p><p>If you’re considering a reverse mortgage or planning to sell your home, I can provide guidance every step of the way. {CM()} to discuss your options.</p></div></section>''')
